 "format": "Commander",
 "name": "Kang the Conqueror: Kang Dynasty",
 "notes": [
  "Plan: Kang is a 4/5 flier for four. His power-up costs {5}{U}{U}{U}, or {3}{U} on a turn he entered, and gives an extra turn. It can be activated once each time he enters, so blinking him resets it.",
  "Brake built into the card: power-up abilities can't be activated during the extra turn, so the most he gives is one extra turn per round. No chaining.",
  "Cheapest line: cast Kang with eight mana available and power up the same turn. After that, each blink (Spaceshift, Essence Flux, Displace, Ghostly Flicker, Illusionist's Stratagem, Wiccan, Silver Surfer, S.H.I.E.L.D. Flying Car, Conjurer's Closet) plus {3}{U} is another turn.",
  "Check with the table whether power-ups can be activated at instant speed before relying on Conjurer's Closet, which blinks at your end step.",
  "Kang variants in the 99: Immortus, Pharaoh Rama-Tut, Victor Timely and Iron Lad, Diverging Destiny, plus the Kang Dynasty Saga. Doom's Time Platform recasts Time Warp from the graveyard for free two turns later.",
  "Archaeomancer with Ghostly Flicker returns the Flicker every time. With Kang as the second target that is an extra turn every round for seven mana. It is bounded by the brake above, but it is the deck's most Bracket 3 moment; say so at the table.",
  "Lightning Greaves is left out on purpose: shroud would stop you blinking Kang.",
  "Ownership tags on each card: have = confirmed owned; freed = from a deck folded Nov 16 or a precon cut; likely = Marvel common or uncommon, or your staples pile; check = owned but maybe sleeved elsewhere; buy = not known to be owned.",
  "Buy list (Nov 12 snapshot): about $24 for the 30 buy cards; Time Warp ($7.37) and Conjurer's Closet ($3.10) are most of it. Estimated, not simulated: wins around turns 9-11 with Kang and fliers in the air over extra turns."
 ],
